# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and build
# artefacts OUT of the image. `.env` is listed explicitly: a stray local env
# file copied into a layer is recoverable from the published image forever.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
# `tsc --build` is incremental: a stale host .tsbuildinfo copied into the image
# makes tsc declare the project up to date and emit NOTHING, so `dist` never
# appears and the runtime COPY fails. Worse, if the stale info ever matched, a
# previous build's output would ship. Never let these into the context.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
playwright-report
test-results
tests
**/test
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
docs
specs
Context
infra
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
